<section begin="intro" />'''Tauron Strike''' is a powerful ability used by the [[Operator]]'s [[Focus]] Schools, functioning as their third ability. It is unlocked after completing [[The Old Peace]] and by purchasing the school's respective [[Tektolyst Artifact]] from [[Marie]]. Five new focus nodes will appear related to the Tauron Strike ability, requiring Focus Points and either {{Resource|Lyroic Bridge}}, {{Resource|Ren Hypercore}}, or {{Resource|Ascaris Prime}} to unlock.<section end="intro" />

==Mechanics==
Tauron Strikes must be charged in order to use. Once charged, the Tauron Strike is activated by the Operator's third ability (default {{Keybind|3}}). This renders the player [[Invulnerable]] as the Operator summons the Warframe to attack with a Tektolyst Artifact. Each Tauron Strike has its damage scaled by the level of the enemy hit using the default [[Enemy Level Scaling#Murmur, Sentient, Anarchs, and Unaffiliated|Enemy Health Scaling Formula]].

[[File:ConvergenceOrbBlue.png|right|x300px|thumb|A Tauron Boost Convergence Orb.]]
There are two ways to charge the Tauron Strike:
*Each enemy killed by the user or an ally within [[Affinity Range]] provides '''0.02%''' charge Tauron Strike. 
*Picking up a {{Resource|Convergence Orb}}, providing '''20%''' charge and multiply all charge gains by '''5x''' while its buff is active.
**If the daily focus cap is reached, a blue version of Convergence Orbs called '''Tauron Boost Convergence Orbs''' will spawn instead, but otherwise have the same bonuses.

===Boosting Charge Rate===
Additionally, each piece of gear equipped with any [[Focus Lens]] will provide a '''10%''' increase in charge gains. Higher tier of focus lens does not grant higher charge rate. Lens applied to the following equipments count towards the effect.
* [[Warframe]]
* [[Primary]]
* [[Secondary]]
* [[Melee]]
* [[Amp]]
* [[Archgun]] (must have [[Archgun Deployer]] equipped in [[Gear]] wheel and the desired Archgun in the Heavy Weapon slot of their [[Arsenal]]'s Gear tab)
* [[K-Drive]] (must have [[K-Drive Launcher]] equipped in Gear wheel)

For example, with a focus lens equipped on primary, secondary, and melee:
*Killing an enemy will give {{MathText|0.02% {{mul}} (1 + 10% {{mul}} 3) {{eql}} 0.026%}} charge. 
*Picking up a Convergence Orb will give {{MathText|20% {{mul}} (1 + 10% {{mul}} 3) {{eql}} 26%}} charge
*With a Convergence Orb buff active, killing an enemy will give {{MathText|0.02% {{mul}} (1 + 10% {{mul}} 3) {{mul}} 5 {{eql}} 0.13%}} charge.

===Case-by-case===
In [[The Perita Rebellion]]:
* Completing one Order will charge the Tauron Strike meter by '''50%'''.
* Fighting [[Hunhullus]], [[Dactolyst]] and [[Prime Vanguard]]s boss fights at the end of the mission will charge the Tauron Strike meter over time.
** If entering the arena with a fully charged Tauron Strike, it will not charge over time after use.
In [[The Guilty]]:
* Player will naturally regenerate [[Tauron Strike]] at the start of every waves of bosses in the game mode. Once used, it will not regenerate until player enters the next wave of bosses. Here are the points where Tauron Strike begins to regenerate:
** The first wave of Prime Vanguards,
** The second wave of Prime Vanguards,
** The third wave of Prime Vanguards,
** The fourth wave of Prime Vanguards,
** The fifth and final wave of Prime Vanguards,
** The start of Dactolyst Duo,
** And the start of Hunhullus.

